SUMMARY:(Day Trip) Blue Ridge Parkway: Blowing Rock Area Hike Plus Fire To
 wer 
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nLet's take a day trip to t
 he mountains in the Blowing Rock area and hike the Flat Top Tower Road Tra
 il near Moses Cone Manor. We'll climb up the fire tower at the end of the 
 trail to take in the beautiful 360 degree view then hike the horse trail l
 eading down to Bass Lake from Moses Cone Manor and back up to the Manor.\n
 \nTotal hiking distance will be about 8 miles. The trails are considered e
 asy to moderate in difficulty. We may need one to two more drivers for thi
 s trip. Depending on interest\, I may increase the attendees by a couple m
 ore people. Please split the cost of gas with your driver.\n\nWe'll meet i
 n Chapel Hill at the MLK Jr. Blvd Harris Teeter parking lot at 6:30AM and 
 leave promptly to try to get to the parking lot before it fills up! Park a
 t the spaces farthest from the entrance of HT. I'll provide further instru
 ctions about the trip once we meet there.\n\nTravel time will be 3 hours. 
 Bring water to stay hydrated\, snacks and lunch.\nAfterwards\, there's an 
 option to make a stop in the Town of Blowing Rock for ice cream before hea
 ding home.\nWe should be back in Chapel Hill by around 8:00PM or earlier.\
 nHoping for good weather. This event may be cancelled if rain is forecast.
 \n\nBy participating in this event\, you agree to the terms below:\n\nTRIP
  PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABILITY I fully realize that this activity involv
 es a risk of personal injury\, property damage\, or loss of my person or p
 roperty. I hereby for myself\, my heirs\, executors and administrators\, a
 nd same for persons with whom are in my party\, waive and release any clai
 ms or rights against Triangle Hiking & Outdoors Group (THOG)\, all of its 
 owners and coordinators for any and all injury\, damages or loss to my per
 son or property incurred during this activity. I also understand that THOG
  organizers are not required\, nor should it be assumed that they are CPR/
 First Aid/Wilderness Survival Certified and I am responsible for my own pe
 rsonal safety.\n\nQuestions? Use the comment section of the event or messa
 ge me.\n\nCheers!\nLarredo
