SUMMARY:(Maine) Acadia Nat’l Park/Partial Solar Eclipse/Perseids Meteor 
 Shower
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\n**Updated information as o
 f 7/22/26:**\nRSVP's will close at 10:00AM on 7/23/26 in order for us to f
 inalize logistics this week.\n\nCome and be a part of one of THOG’s most
  ambitious trips. This summer adventure in Maine includes Acadia National 
 Park and Bar Harbor\, as well as two amazing celestial events- A partial S
 olar Eclipse and the Perseids Meteor Shower.\nThis exciting road trip even
 t will be slightly different from other THOG events. We will be partnering
  with Wanderful Journeys\, a local travel club that hosts trips to various
  destinations. I decided to team up with them so it would provide us with 
 another layer of resources for planning\, as well as to enhance the trip e
 xperience.\n**See RSVP requirements below before you register**.\n\n**High
 lights of our weeklong trip will include:**\n-Hikes in Acadia National Par
 k such as Precipice Trail and Beehive Trail\n-Thunder Hole\n-Jordan Pond\n
 -Maine Lobster :)\n-Lighthouses in Maine\n-Viewing the partial Solar Eclip
 se\n-Watching the Perseids Meteor Shower (up to 100 per hour this year)\n-
 Exploring Bar Harbor\n-Bar Island Trail hike- a trail that appears only du
 ring low tide\n-Exclusive Swag options for trip participants\n\n**Here is 
 a brief overview of our itinerary on this trip** which is subject to chang
 e depending on weather and/or other factors:\n8/9- Carpools will meet in a
  central location in the Triangle and begin Day 1 of our trip with an over
 night stop at a hotel in NJ\n8/10- Continue our trip with a featured stop 
 along the way at Portland Head Light then arrive at Acadia Nat'l Park/Bar 
 Harbor for either camping or hotel stay\n8/11- Sunrise at Cadillac Mountai
 n\, hiking choices in Acadia and other activities then dinner at camp or i
 n Bar Harbor\n8/12- **Solar Eclipse/Perseids Meteor Shower Day Activities:
 ** *Watch partial Solar Eclipse* near Otter Point\, Explore Bar Harbor\, *
 Late-night* *viewing of Perseids Meteor Shower* near campground at the coa
 st\n8/13- Activities: Sunrise and hike at Otter Point\, Bar Island Trail h
 ike\, Thunder Hole\, Jordan Pond\, Sunset at Bass Harbor Head Light Statio
 n\n8/14- Head back to NJ to our hotel with a featured stop along the way.\
 n8/15- Continue our trip back home with a featured stop along the way.\nAl
 l participants will be required to pay a $100 deposit to secure their spot
  on this trip.\n**Accommodations overview:** Everyone will be staying at a
  designated hotel in NJ going to Maine and returning from Maine.\nIn Maine
 \, you will have two stay options:\n-designated Group Campsites (4 nights)
  that has modern bathrooms\; paid showers are located nearby\n-designated 
 hotel in Bar Harbor (4 nights) two beds per room\nIf you choose the hotel 
 stay in Maine\, it is crucial that you submit your deposit as soon as you 
 RSVP (see rsvp requirements below) to secure your hotel spot due to limite
 d room availability. Roommate info/rules will also be in a link that will 
 be sent to all who RSVP.\n**Estimated Costs:**\nThe costs below include tr
 ansportation (gas\, tolls\, parking)\, National Park passes\, Hotel stays 
 during travel\nCamping- $600-$650 per person\nHotel- $1\,100-$1\,150 per p
 erson\nThese best estimates may change depending on the number of attendee
 s and could decrease or increase. We will notify you of any changes.\n\n**
 important RSVP requirements:**\n\n1. You will be asked a **three-part ques
 tion** as you are RSVPing for this event. **Please answer completely**!\n2
 . After you RSVP to this trip\, you will be sent a **link to your email** 
 **address** that will have questions you need to answer as well as a link 
 to pay your **$100 deposit (required for every trip participant)**. Links 
 will have all the information about the trip\, total costs per person\, ru
 les on how the deposit works\, itinerary\, trip expectations\, and swag in
 formation.\nYour spot on this trip will not be guaranteed until the deposi
 t is paid.\n\nTRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABILITY I fully realize that th
 is activity involves a risk of personal injury\, property damage\, or loss
  of my person or property. I hereby for myself\, my heirs\, executors and 
 administrators\, and same for persons with whom are in my party\, waive an
 d release any claims or rights against Triangle Hiking & Outdoors Group (T
 HOG)\, all of its owners and coordinators for any and all injury\, damages
  or loss to my person or property incurred during this activity. I also un
 derstand that THOG organizers are not required\, nor should it be assumed 
 that they are CPR/First Aid/Wilderness Survival Certified and I am respons
 ible for my own personal safety.\n\nWe look forward to having you be a par
 t of this adventure!\nIf you have any questions\, please send me (Larredo)
  a meetup message or comment below if it is something that could benefit t
 he group. Thanks!\nSee you all soon!\nLarredo and Geniece
